  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Mainly dry, tranquil and cooler weather pattern \nexpected into the last weekend of July \n\nCool cyclonic/WNW flow aloft will trigger light rain shower \nactivity today downwind of Lake Erie over the Allegheny \nPlateau. Hires guidance shows low clouds/stratocu slow to erode\nthis morning over the western high terrain. Exiting cold front \ncould trigger an isolated PM t-storm over the far southeast part\nof the CWA, but precip odds are less than 20%. SPC has shifted \nthe level 1/5 MRGL risk out of Lancaster County to the I95 \ncorridor. Max temps in the mid 60s to mid 70s over the \nAlleghenies are 5 to 15 degrees below the historical average for\nlate July. The relatively cool daytime temps today will be \nenhanced by a noticeable WNW breeze gusting 20-25 mph. Mainly \nclear skies expected tonight with below climo to chilly min \ntemps for this time of year fcst in the 40-60F range from NW to \nSE. Areas of valley fog are expected late tonight into early \nThursday morning. \n\nThe cooler/less humid airmass will usher in a dry spell into the\nlast weekend of July with high pressure in control. Upper trough\ncarving out over the eastern Great Lakes into the Northeast US\nwill bring rain chances back into the forecast Sunday into next\nweek.",
